                                 The plant-based protein flours exhibit promising nutritional profiles, rich in proteins,
                           essential fatty acids, and minerals, and low in harmful contaminants such as PAHs and
                           heavy metals. These findings support the potential of these flours as sustainable and
                           healthful ingredients in the food industry. The high protein content of coffee grounds and
                           spent brewer’s yeast flours, in particular, highlights their significant potential as novel
                           sources of plant-based protein.

